/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.Rmd-502-$$Y_{i,t} = \alpha_i + \alpha_t + \gamma_k^{-K}~ D_{i,t}^{<-K} + \sum_{k=-K}^{-2} \gamma_k^{lead} D_{i,t}^{k} +\sum_{k=0}^{L}  \gamma_k^{lag} D_{i,t}^{k} + \gamma_k^{L+} D_{i,t}^{>L} + \varepsilon_{i,t}$$
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.Rmd-503-with $K$ and $L$ set to 5. That is, binning the endpoints.
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.Rmd-504-
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.Rmd:505:As you can see from the results below, the biases are still substantial. Thus, the problems with TWFE specifications persist even if you have a "never-treated" group.
