/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/did-basics.html-377-there are going to be 4 time periods. There are 4000 units in the
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/did-basics.html-378-treated group that are randomly (with equal probability) assigned to
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/did-basics.html-379-first participate in the treatment (a <em>group</em>) in each time
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/did-basics.html:380:period. And there are 4000 ``never treated’’ units. The data generating
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/did-basics.html-381-process for untreated potential outcomes</p>
