/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.html-705-cohort. Furthermore, since covariates are not available (and do not play
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.html-706-any major role into the analysis), we do not need to worry about the
--
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.html-772-<p>One of the features of the above DGP is that all units eventually get
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.html-773-treated. In some applications, we have that a group of units remain
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.html-774-untreated at the end of the sample. We call this group of units the
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.html:775:“never-treated” group. To assess if the problems associated with TWFE
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.html-776-specification highlighted above persist if such a group of units is
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.html-777-available, we modify a little bit the DGP and repeat the same exercise
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.html-778-as above.</p>
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.html:779:<div id="dgp-with-a-never-treated-group-and-homogeneous-treatment-effect-dynamics" class="section level3">
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.html:780:<h3>DGP with a “never-treated” group and homogeneous treatment effect
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.html-781-dynamics</h3>
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.html-782-<p>The DGP we consider is very similar to the one we have already
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.html-783-considered. The only difference is that now we suppress treatment for
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.html:784:the last cohort. Put it simply, the cohort with <span class="math inline">\(g=2004\)</span> is now “never-treated”, implying
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.html-785-that, in this DGP the unit-specific treatment effects at time <span class="math inline">\(t\)</span> <span class="math inline">\(\tau_{i,t}\)</span> are generated as <span class="math display">\[ \tau_{i,t} = \mu \times (t - g + 1)\times 1\{t
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.html-786-\ge g \}1\{g\not=2004 \},\]</span> where <span class="math inline">\(\mu\)</span> is the the instantaneous treatment
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.html-787-effect; we set <span class="math inline">\(\mu=1\)</span>.</p>
