/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/did-basics.Rmd-293-There are a few things to notice in this case
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/did-basics.Rmd-294-
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/did-basics.Rmd-295-* There does not appear to be much evidence against the parallel trends assumption.  One fails to reject using the Wald test reported in `summary`; likewise the uniform confidence bands cover 0 in all pre-treatment periods.
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/did-basics.Rmd-296-
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/did-basics.Rmd:297:* There is some evidence of negative effects of the minimum wage on employment.  Two group-time average treatment effects are negative and statistically different from 0.  These results also suggest that it may be helpful to aggregate the group-time average treatment effects.
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/did-basics.Rmd-298-
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/did-basics.Rmd-299-```{r,  fig.width=8,fig.height=5, fig.align='center', out.width="90%", dpi = 200}
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/did-basics.Rmd-300-# aggregate the group-time average treatment effects
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/did-basics.Rmd-301-mw.dyn <- aggte(mw.attgt, type = "dynamic")
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/did-basics.Rmd-302-summary(mw.dyn)
