/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.Rmd:672:In this specific DGP, as there is a "never-treated" group, we can use use different comparison groups: 1) the "never-treated" group, and 2) the "not-yet-treated" group. In this particular DGP, using any of these two different comparison groups should recover the true underlying dynamic treatment effect. Let's see if this is indeed the case.
