/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.Rmd-905-
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.Rmd-906-### Estimating dynamic treatment effects via TWFE event-study regressions
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.Rmd-907-
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.Rmd-908-Like before, we start by estimating a TWFE event-study regression 
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.Rmd-909-$$Y_{i,t} = \alpha_i + \alpha_t + \gamma_k^{-K}~ D_{i,t}^{<-K} + \sum_{k=-K}^{-2} \gamma_k^{lead} D_{i,t}^{k} +\sum_{k=0}^{L}  \gamma_k^{lag} D_{i,t}^{k} + \gamma_k^{L+} D_{i,t}^{>L} + \varepsilon_{i,t}$$
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.Rmd-910-with $K$ and $L$ set to 5. That is, binning the endpoints.
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.Rmd-911-
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.Rmd-912-As you can see from the results below, the biases are still substantial. Given the results we have shown before, this should not be a surprise.
--
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.Rmd-1064-
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.Rmd-1065-ES_plot_sat_never_het
