/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.Rmd-1071-
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.Rmd:1072:As the result above shows, when treatment effects dynamics are heterogeneous across groups, TWFE event-study regressions do not recover the true underlying dynamic treatment effects, even if a "never-treated" group is available and one does not bin extreme event-times. Again, this is a red flag for the usage of TWFE-type regressions in DiD setups. 
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.Rmd-1073-
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.Rmd-1074-### Using the Callaway and Sant'Anna (2021) framework
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.Rmd-1075-
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.Rmd-1076-Next, we show that the procedure put forward by Callaway and Sant'Anna (2021) and implemented in our **did** can also be used in this setup. In other words, Callaway and Sant'Anna (2021) proposal *does not rely on restricting treatment effect heterogeneity*.
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.Rmd-1077-
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.Rmd-1078-
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.Rmd:1079:First, let's estimate the treatment effect dynamics using the "never-treated" units as the comparison group.
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.Rmd-1080-
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.Rmd-1081-```{r CS_never_het, message = FALSE, warning = FALSE, cache = TRUE, cache.lazy = TRUE, fig.width=8,fig.height=5, fig.align='center', out.width="90%", dpi = 200}
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.Rmd-1082-# function to run ES DID
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.Rmd-1083-run_CS_never_het <- function(...) {
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.Rmd-1084-  
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.Rmd-1085-  # resimulate the data
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.Rmd-1086-  data <- make_data3()
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.Rmd-1087-  data$cohort_year[data$cohort_year==Inf] <- 0
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.Rmd-1088-  
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.Rmd-1089-  mod <- did::att_gt(yname = "dep_var", 
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.Rmd-1090-                     tname = "year",
/opt/homebrew/lib/R/4.5/site-library/did/doc/TWFE.Rmd-1091-                     idname = "unit",
